<title>NEW ZEALAND: Steel&amp;Tube interim profit slips 3 percent.</title>
<headline>Steel&amp;Tube interim profit slips 3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five months to Nov 30</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   10.96 vs 11.38</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			     25 vs 26</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			   20.0 vs 20.0</p>
<p>    Turnover			     187.6 vs 133.3</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			 17.7 vs 17.4</p>
<p>    Tax					6.5 vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)   43.96 million vs 43.66</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credits.</p>
<p>Pay date March 12</p>
<p>Reg date February 28</p>
<p>Note - Steel and Tube Ltd is a steel parts manufacturer half owned by Tubemakers of Australia Ltd in which the Broken Hill Pty Ltd has a controlling interest.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
